Actor. State machine instance. Holds everything.

Current state. Mutable context. Transition handlers. Effects. Clock. Children.

## Make actor

```ts
import { Actor, state, event } from "@mantaq/core";

const idle = state("idle")();
const active = state("active")();

const activate = event("ACTIVATE")();

const actor = new Actor({
  inputs: [activate],
  states: [idle, active],
  initial: idle,
  transitions: {
    idle: {
      ACTIVATE: () => ({ state: active }),
    },
  },
});
```

## Send events

```ts
actor.send(activate.create());
```

Events. Plain objects. `id` field required. `event.create(payload)` makes them.

## Check state

```ts
import { matches } from "@mantaq/sugar";

matches(actor, "active"); // true
```

## Listen for changes

```ts
const unsub = actor.on("change", (snapshot) => {
  console.log("New state:", snapshot.path);
});

// Call unsub() to stop
```

Fires immediately. Current snapshot.

## Settled

```ts
await actor.settled();
```

Waits. Internal events drained. Use after effects.

## Snapshot

```ts
actor.snapshot();
// { path: ["active"], regions: {}, done: undefined }
```

State tree. Nested for hierarchical actors.

## Constructor options

| Option           | Type                    | What                                 |
| ---------------- | ----------------------- | ------------------------------------ |
| `inputs`         | `EventRef[]`            | External events accepted             |
| `outputs`        | `EventRef[]`            | Events to parent                     |
| `internal`       | `EventRef[]`            | Events from effects/transitions      |
| `states`         | `StateRef[]`            | All states                           |
| `initial`        | `StateRef`              | Start state                          |
| `context`        | `object`                | Mutable context                      |
| `transitions`    | `object`                | State/event map                      |
| `effects`        | `object`                | Side effects per state               |
| `clock`          | `Clock`                 | Default: `RealClock`                 |
| `regions`        | `Record<string, Actor>` | Static children                      |
| `internalBudget` | `number`                | Max internal events (default: 10000) |

Context. Mutable record. Survives transitions. Holds data.

## Define context

Pass object to Actor constructor.

```ts
type CounterContext = { count: number };

const actor = new Actor({
  inputs: [increment, decrement],
  states: [idle],
  initial: idle,
  context: { count: 0 } as CounterContext,
  transitions: {
    idle: {
      INCREMENT: (_, { context }) => {
        context.count++;
        return {};
      },
    },
  },
```

`{} as CounterContext`. Type safety. No runtime cost.

## Read context

```ts
actor.context.count; // 0
```

Getter returns `Readonly<T>`. Handlers get mutable reference.

## Context in transitions

Handler gets context directly.

```ts
transitions: {
  idle: {
    LOGIN: (event, { context }) => {
      context.username = event.username;
      context.attempts++;
      return { state: authenticating };
    },
  },
}
```

## Context in effects

Effects get context too.

```ts
effects: {
  authenticating: [
    ({ context, emit }) => {
      authenticate(context.username).then(
        (result) => emit({ id: "AUTH_DONE", result }),
      );
    },
  ],
}
```

## Context in children

Child actors. Own context. Communicate via events.

